-- ============================================================
-- Seed data for a freshly reset database.
--
-- `supabase migration squash` captures schema only, so the rows that the old
-- migration chain inserted along the way were lost when 94 files collapsed into
-- one baseline. Three of those sets are not sample data but requirements:
--
--   * storage.buckets — without them every upload path fails: product images,
--     banner images, review photos and return photos all target a bucket by id.
--   * delivery_zones  — checkout prices delivery from this table; an empty one
--     leaves the customer unable to complete an order.
--   * categories      — the catalogue's category filter has nothing to show.
--
-- Only sample products and banners remain here. What the application actually
-- requires - storage buckets, delivery zones, categories - moved to migration
-- 20260814010000_functional_reference_data.sql, because seed.sql runs only on a
-- local `supabase db reset` and never reaches a deployed project.
--
-- Deliberately NOT seeded: admin_accounts. The old migration inserted
-- admin@shop.uz / Admin123 and two more in plaintext into a `password_plain`
-- column that a later migration removed — so it would fail today, and shipping
-- default credentials in a committed file is not something to carry forward.
-- Create the first admin explicitly, letting the database hash the password:
--
--   INSERT INTO admin_accounts (email, first_name, role, is_active, password_hash)
--   VALUES ('you@example.com', 'Name', 'super_admin', true,
--           hash_admin_password('<a real password>')) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
--
-- config.toml already points [db.seed] at this file, so `supabase db reset`
-- runs it automatically.
-- ============================================================

